/-!
# Boolean Sum-of-Squares Strong Duality and the Atserias–Hakoniemi Size-Degree Trade-Off

This module proves Boolean Sum-of-Squares strong duality in even degree and the Atserias–Hakoniemi
 exponential size-degree trade-off for Sum-of-Squares refutations over `ℝ`, under standard
Lean constraints.

1. **Boolean SoS strong duality**: for any finite set of Boolean variables `σ`, any polynomial
   system `F` containing `X i ^ 2 - X i` for all `i : σ`, and any `m ≥ 1`, if `F` admits no
   degree-`2 * m` SoS refutation, then `1` lies in the interior of the truncated degree-`2 * m`
   SoS cone, so geometric Hahn–Banach separation produces a degree-`2 * m`
   `Cslib.Logic.PL.SOS.PseudoExpectation F (2 * m)`.
2. **Full-degree Boolean zero-variance absorption**: if a degree-`2 * r` Boolean
   pseudo-expectation satisfies `Ẽ (1 - X w) = 0`, then `Ẽ ((1 - X w) * q) = 0` for every
   polynomial `q` of total degree at most `2 * r - 1`, restricting `X w ← 1` with zero degree
   loss.
3. **Atserias–Hakoniemi size-degree trade-off**: any Boolean polynomial system `F` over `n ≥ 1`
   variables of degree at most `k` that has no SoS refutation of degree strictly less than `d`
   (`k ≤ d`) satisfies `Real.exp ((d - k) ^ 2 / (600 * n)) ≤ π.size` for every SoS refutation
   `π` of `F` (and `Real.exp ((d - k) ^ 2 / (1200 * N)) ≤ π.size` for twin-literal systems over
   at most `N ≥ 1` active variable pairs).

## Main results

* `CslibFrontier.ProofComplexity.exists_pseudoExpectation_of_not_refutableInDegree`: Boolean SoS
  strong duality in even degree `2 * m` (`1 ≤ m`).
* `CslibFrontier.ProofComplexity.atserias_hakoniemi_size_degree`: Atserias–Hakoniemi exponential
  size-degree trade-off over `n` Boolean variables.
* `CslibFrontier.ProofComplexity.atserias_hakoniemi_size_degree_twin`: twin-literal specialization
  in
  terms of an upper bound `N` on the number of active variable pairs.
-/

public section

